/-
Submission history. On 27 November 2026 at 11:39 UTC, Michael Devine
submitted a locally kernel-verified Lean proof of 85.5002389618% under RH
using a quadratic mollifier taper and a prime/semiprime detector. At
13:47 UTC the leaderboard verifier returned verification-timeout.

On 26 November 2026 at 19:45 UTC, we applied Yuanda Xu's simple-zero
estimate to our distinct-zero count. At 22:28 UTC we had recorded the
joint certificate construction from which the present variant descends.
On 27 November at 18:17 UTC we recorded the certificate for this variant,
which sets the weight of the separate simple-zero estimate to zero.

We derived this certificate independently of Kristian Muri Knausgaard's
85.5366277780% argument. The comparison theorem uses that result's score
as the previous record. We credit his earlier Lean foundations below.
-/

